# Styling Conventions

## Stack

- SCSS Modules (`.module.scss`) for all component styles; `globals.scss` for CSS custom properties, resets and base styles.
- No Tailwind or utility classes, no BEM, no CSS-in-JS (styled-components, emotion, inline style objects), no plain CSS.

## Files

- Every component has a `.module.scss` in its own folder (`components/ChatBox/ChatBox.module.scss`). Page-level styles are `camelCase.module.scss` (`tripDetail.module.scss`).
- Global styles live in `globals.scss` (`src/app/globals.scss` in Next, `assets/css/main.scss` in Nuxt, `styles/globals.scss` in Vite). Shared partials (`_variables.scss`, `_mixins.scss`) live in `src/styles/` and are imported with `@use`.
- Import the module as `styles` in both frameworks: `import styles from './ChatBox.module.scss'` (in Vue, inside `<script setup>`; never a `<style module>` block).
- Compose classes with template literals in TSX, `` `${styles.chip} ${selected ? styles.chipSelected : ''}` ``, and with the array form in Vue, `:class="[styles.chip, isSelected && styles.chipSelected]"`. No `classnames` or `clsx`.

## Tokens

- Define every color as a kebab-case CSS custom property on `:root` in `globals.scss` and use `var(--name)`. Never hardcode hex values in component SCSS (pure white `#fff` and error red `#ef4444` are the exceptions).
- Name tokens for purpose, not appearance: `--accent`, `--foreground-muted`, `--surface-hover`, `--border`, not `--blue`.
- Theme by switching the tokens under a `data-theme` attribute on `<html>`.

## Classes and nesting

- Class names are camelCase: `.chatBox`, `.messageList`. No `__` or `--`, no kebab-case.
- Variants are separate classes (`.chip` plus `.chipSelected`); state classes are camelCase too (`.active`, `.disabled`). The screen-reader-only class is `.srOnly`. Keyframes are camelCase (`typingDot`).
- Nest for pseudo-classes and elements, parent-context selectors (`.user .bubble`), direct child elements and compound selectors via `&`. Maximum two levels deep (pseudo-classes excluded); flatten into a new class beyond that.

```scss
.navLink {
    padding: 8px 16px;
    color: var(--foreground-muted);
    transition: background 0.15s, color 0.15s;

    &:hover { background: var(--surface-hover); color: var(--foreground); }
    &.active { background: var(--surface-active); font-weight: 600; }
}
```

## Layout and scale

- Desktop-first with `max-width` media queries, placed together at the bottom of the module. Breakpoints: `$bp-mobile: 480px`, `$bp-tablet: 800px`, `$bp-desktop: 1200px`.
- Use `px`. Spacing scale: 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 48, 64, 80. Radius: 4 subtle, 8 standard, 10 buttons, 12 cards, 16 large cards, 20 pills, 50% circles.
- Max content width 1400px with `margin: 0 auto`; page padding 24px horizontal, 16px on mobile.
- Body font `var(--font-geist-sans), system-ui, sans-serif` at 14px. Sizes: 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 18, 20, 28, 32, 48. Weights 400, 500, 600, 700 (800 for hero titles only). Line height 1.5 for body, 1.6 for paragraphs, 1.1 for heroes.
- Transitions: `0.15s` for hover, `0.2s` for state changes, default easing.

## Interactive elements

- Set `font-family: inherit` and `cursor: pointer` on clickable elements.
- Handle `:disabled` with `opacity: 0.5` and `cursor: not-allowed`, and use `:hover:not(:disabled)` so disabled controls do not react to hover.
- Inputs: `outline: none` with a `border-color: var(--accent)` change on `:focus`; placeholder uses `var(--foreground-muted)`.
- Global reset in `globals.scss`: `* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }`, links `color: inherit; text-decoration: none`, body color and background from tokens, `html, body { max-width: 100vw; overflow-x: hidden; }`.

## Formatting

- 4-space indent, one declaration per line, opening brace on the selector line, trailing semicolons, blank line between rules.
- Order properties by box model: position, display, sizing, spacing, border, background, typography, transition or animation.
- In files over 100 lines, group rules under `/* ---- Section Name ---- */` comments.
